# FABLE-SONNET-OWN-LOOKUP-AUDIT-20260923-131 Part 2, negative. `beta` reads
# `shared` as a dynamic input with its own eventual binding line (so it is
# a legitimate dynamic input, not merely an unresolved name -- that earlier,
# separate check fires first for a name with no binding anywhere at all,
# measured directly: a callee that never binds the name anywhere in its own
# body is refused "unresolved name" at the READ site, before l2_hidden_from
# ever runs. This is the existing definition of a dynamic input, not a gap
# this ticket found or touches). `gamma` calls beta with no
# binding for `shared` either, so `shared` becomes gamma's OWN (pass-
# through) dynamic input too -- and gamma never binds it anywhere in
# itself. l2_hidden_from's fallback, computing what gamma forwards to beta
# at the entry->gamma call site, resolves the name in gamma's own table
# (l2_own_find scoped to gamma) and finds nothing: a located refusal
# naming gamma, never a silent 0 and never some other method's field.
fn: beta () int
    c.printf: "beta sees shared=%d\n" shared
    int: shared 222
    return: 0
end: beta

fn: gamma () int
    beta()
    return: 0
end: gamma

gamma()
return: 0
